    "Two-component diffusion: 1st translational diffusion only, 2nd Translational and rotational diffusion":
        {
            "Function_description":"User-defined function: The model describes the diffusion in a system composed of two diffusing species where one of the species undergoes rotations in a timescale comparable to the timescale of translational diffusion across the focal volume.\nParameters description:\nG_inf - offset\nN_p - Number of fluorescent molecules\nq - amplitude of diffusing species\nA2 -Second, non zero amplitude for rotation\nA4 - fourth , non-zero amplitude for rotation\nf - fraction relating the rotational to translational diffusion for a given diffusing species.\nA = pi * k_B\nT - Absolute temperature\neta_R1 - Rotational viscosity experienced by the first diffusing species\neta_T1 - Translational viscosity experienced by the first diffusing species\neta_T2 - Translational viscosity experienced by the second diffusing species\nr_1 - Hydrodynamic radius of the first diffusing species \nr_2 - Hydrodynamic radius of the second diffusing species\nomega_0 - Width of the focal volume\nkappa - Structure parameter",
